			<div class="content" id="post-content-2278994">
									

<p>Well, if we're talking about the ballpark here, a 761-mile-radius circle has an area of about 4.7 million square kilometers &#8212; probably a bit more, given that it's on a sphere so it'll bulge. The Earth's total surface area is about 510 million square kilometers. The math is such that to be absolutely certain that someone isn't gonna get their fill of 449 when all are going, there should be 109 of them.</p>
<p>Incidentally, what pressure does the 449-A come out at when the cone's going at full tilt? I'm imagining someone using one of these like an improvised water cannon and laughing.</p>
<p>Also,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>To date, all individuals SCP-449 instances have been recovered from had gone to extreme lengths</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd recommend changing that to &quot;all individuals from which SCP-449 instances have been recovered&quot;. It reads better.</p>

